### ================================================================
### FASE 6 — Simulación de Nota Objetivo (AIB-17)
### Prerequisito: fases 1, 2, 3 y 4 ejecutadas (fase 5 es opcional)
###
### Estado de la BD al llegar aquí (subject id=1):
###   cutId=5  Corte 1  30%  grade=5.00  → calificado
###   cutId=6  Corte 2  30%  grade=3.50  → calificado
###   cutId=7  Corte 3  40%  grade=null  → PENDIENTE
###
### Fórmula de simulación:
###   currentScore      = 5.00*30 + 3.50*30 = 255
###   pendingPercentage = 40
###   requiredGrade     = (targetGrade*100 - 255) / 40
### ================================================================

@baseUrl = https://aibert-academic-service-qa.yellowwave-cb2d91fc.centralus.azurecontainerapps.io
@studentId = test-student-123
@ct = application/json
@s1 = 1
@cut3 = 7


# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CASO 1 — Error: materia inexistente → 404 Not Found
# Espera: { "success": false, "error": "Materia con id 999 no encontrada", "code": 404 }
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
### POST simulate en subjectId=999
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/subjects/999/simulate
Content-Type: {{ct}}
studentId: {{studentId}}

{
  "targetGrade": 3.5
}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CASO 2 — Error: targetGrade fuera de rango (> 5.0) → 400 Bad Request
# Espera: { "success": false, "error": "La nota objetivo no puede superar 5.0", "code": 400 }
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
### POST simulate con targetGrade=6.0
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/subjects/{{s1}}/simulate
Content-Type: {{ct}}
studentId: {{studentId}}

{
  "targetGrade": 6.0
}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CASO 3 — Error: targetGrade negativo → 400 Bad Request
# Espera: error de validación @DecimalMin
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
### POST simulate con targetGrade=-1.0
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/subjects/{{s1}}/simulate
Content-Type: {{ct}}
studentId: {{studentId}}

{
  "targetGrade": -1.0
}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CASO 4 — Error: targetGrade nulo → 400 Bad Request
# Espera: { "success": false, "error": "La nota objetivo no puede ser nula", "code": 400 }
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
### POST simulate con targetGrade=null
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/subjects/{{s1}}/simulate
Content-Type: {{ct}}
studentId: {{studentId}}

{
  "targetGrade": null
}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CASO 5 — Meta alcanzable → 200 OK  isAchievable=true
# targetGrade=4.0
# requiredGrade = (4.0*100 - 255) / 40 = 145/40 = 3.625
# Espera:
#   requiredGrade=3.625
#   isAchievable=true
#   pendingCuts=[{ cutId: 7, cutName: "Corte 3", cutPercentage: 40 }]
#   message="Para alcanzar 4.0 necesitas obtener 3.63 o más..."
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
### POST simulate targetGrade=4.0 — meta alcanzable
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/subjects/{{s1}}/simulate
Content-Type: {{ct}}
studentId: {{studentId}}

{
  "targetGrade": 4.0
}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CASO 6 — Meta inalcanzable → 200 OK  isAchievable=false
# targetGrade=5.0
# requiredGrade = (5.0*100 - 255) / 40 = 245/40 = 6.125  → supera 5.0
# Espera:
#   requiredGrade=6.125
#   isAchievable=false
#   pendingCuts=[{ cutId: 7, cutName: "Corte 3", cutPercentage: 40 }]
#   message="No es posible alcanzar 5.0. La nota requerida (6.13) supera el máximo..."
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
### POST simulate targetGrade=5.0 — meta inalcanzable
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/subjects/{{s1}}/simulate
Content-Type: {{ct}}
studentId: {{studentId}}

{
  "targetGrade": 5.0
}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CASO 7 — Meta ya asegurada → 200 OK  isAchievable=true  requiredGrade=0.0
# targetGrade=2.0
# requiredGrade = (2.0*100 - 255) / 40 = -55/40 = -1.375 → clampeado a 0.0
# Ya se supera la meta sin importar la nota del Corte 3
# Espera:
#   requiredGrade=0.0
#   isAchievable=true
#   pendingCuts=[{ cutId: 7, cutName: "Corte 3", cutPercentage: 40 }]
#   message="¡Ya tienes asegurado superar tu meta!..."
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
### POST simulate targetGrade=2.0 — meta ya asegurada
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/subjects/{{s1}}/simulate
Content-Type: {{ct}}
studentId: {{studentId}}

{
  "targetGrade": 2.0
}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Setup para CASO 8: registrar nota en Corte 3 (el último pendiente)
# gradeId=4 (o el siguiente disponible), cutId=7, 100%
# Tras este POST, subject id=1 no tiene cortes pendientes
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
### POST nota en Corte 3 — cierra todos los cortes
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/subjects/{{s1}}/cuts/{{cut3}}/grades
Content-Type: {{ct}}
studentId: {{studentId}}

{
  "activityName": "Examen Final",
  "gradeValue": 3.8,
  "percentage": 100
}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CASO 8 — Sin cortes pendientes → 422 Unprocessable Entity
# Todos los cortes tienen nota; no hay qué simular
# Espera: { "success": false,
#            "error": "La materia con id 1 no tiene cortes pendientes por calificar",
#            "code": 422 }
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
### POST simulate sin cortes pendientes
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/subjects/{{s1}}/simulate
Content-Type: {{ct}}
studentId: {{studentId}}

{
  "targetGrade": 3.5
}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CASO 9 — Verificar promedio final de la materia → 200 OK
# Con los 3 cortes calificados:
#   Corte 1: 5.00 * 30 = 150
#   Corte 2: 3.50 * 30 = 105
#   Corte 3: 3.80 * 40 = 152
#   overallAverage = (150 + 105 + 152) / 100 = 4.07
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
### GET averages finales con los 3 cortes calificados
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/subjects/{{s1}}/averages
studentId: {{studentId}}
